"Leaf 12. The three words at the top read: \"This is Nature.\" The lines above the donkey read: \"This is the Philosophers' donkey who wished to rise to the practice of the Philosopher's Stone.\" The three lines below the animal are translated: \"Frogs gather in multitudes but science consists of clear water made from the Sun and Moon.\" The text under the symbolic bird is as follows: \"This is fortune with two wings. Whosoever has it knows that fruit will in such a way be produced. A great philosopher has shown that the stone is a certain white sun, to see which needs a telescope. To dissolve it in water requires the Sun and Moon, and here one must open 200 telescopes, putting body and soul in one mass. And here is lost the mass; other sages cook the frogs and add nothing, if the juice of the Wise you wish to enjoy.\" To the Greeks the frog symbolized both metempsychosis and earthly humidity."
